WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:39.080
[Music]

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:46.820
[Children play on the steps and in the courtyard outside a school.]

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:53.640
[Narrator:] Hello. Here are Mary Jane and
Tommy Davis. Let's follow them into the classroom.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:01:05.980
[Children make their way up the school steps and into the classroom, finding their desks.]

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:12.020
[Narrator:] Shh. Miss Allen is going to speak. She gives out special project assignments on sleep,

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:17.000
good posture, and Mary Jane and Tommy are assigned mouth health.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.240
[Children come down the steps, leaving the classroom.]

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:26.540
[Narrator:] They wonder what in the world they can do with a subject on mouth health. 

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.960
The study of oral hygiene just doesn't seem to suggest anything for a project. 

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:36.220
They don't realize how interesting it really can be.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:42.580
[The two children walk down the street, puzzling over their assigned topic.]

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:46.800
[Narrator:] Of course! Their friend, Dr. Wilson, the family dentist will help them.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:54.360
[Mary Jane and Tommy see the dentist's sign and dash towards Dr. Wilson's office.]

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:59.000
[Narrator:] Hmm. Wonder if he's busy.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:02.920
[Mary Jane and Tommy peer into the office, noses pressed against the window.]

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:06.860
[Narrator:] Miss Young, the dental assistant, welcomes Mary Jane and Tommy.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.100
They tell her about their project assignment. 

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.520
The dentist, Dr. Wilson,
has just finished cleaning Carol's teeth,

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.360
as he has done every four months since she was two years old.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:24.200
Since the dentist is busy, Miss Young takes
the children into the waiting room

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:29.520
to show them a book which may suggest some ideas for their project.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.760
Each year, Carol has had an x-ray of her teeth, which would have shown a dark spot if she had had a small cavity .

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:44.420
The x-ray is a detective,
which indicates the positions of the permanent teeth,

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:49.340
which are forming here below the first,
or deciduous, teeth .

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:55.500
This early detection helps to prevent larger
and more expensive fillings later.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:02.200
In the meantime, Miss Young has been showing the children pictures of the first, or deciduous,

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:07.200
teeth of a six-year-old child. The permanent teeth are forming at the ends of the roots

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.520
of the deciduous teeth, as we noticed in the x-ray.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:16.320
[ Music ]

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:22.060
[Narrator:] Miss Young suggests that since tomorrow is a holiday, she will take them to see the orthodontist,

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.620
Dr. Martin, who has many dental models and charts.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:30.340
And besides, Dr. Martin may even let them ride his son's pony.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:34.420
[The children approach the gate of Dr. Martin's home, where a sign reads Happy Hollow,]

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.860
[Narrator:] Well, here they are at Dr. Martin's home office.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.360
Looks as if his son, Scotty, is getting a pony ride.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.300
[ Music ]

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:49.640
[Narrator:] Miss Young will go with Scotty so that Dr. Martin can take more time from his

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:54.780
laboratory work to show the children the exhibits. Let's listen in.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.820
[Dr. Martin:] In this exhibit, Mary Jane and
Tommy, 

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:01.020
notice how the shape of the face changes as the jaws and teeth develop.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.080
At birth, teeth are already forming in the
jaws. 

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:08.560
Yet the first tooth doesn't appear in the mouth until about six months of age.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:11.280
[Several models and posters of teeth and jaws are displayed.]

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:15.680
[Dr. Martin:] Between five-and-a-half to seven-and-a-half years of age, the first permanent, 

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.000
or sixth-year, molars make their appearance, back of all the first teeth.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.400
They are the most important, since they influence the position of all the other teeth.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:33.060
At 14 years of age, the shape of the face
has taken on adult proportions. 

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:39.540
All the permanent teeth are in the mouth, with the exception of the third molars, or wisdom teeth,

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:43.160
which come in sometime after the 17th year.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.060
[ Music ]

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:52.940
[Dr. Martin:] So let's go into the garden and discuss these models of children's teeth.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.660
They're good examples of orthodontics, or the straightening of teeth.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.340
[Mary Jane, Tommy, and the orthodontist sit down at a table in the garden, under a tree.]

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:03.940
[Dr. Martin:] Now here's a picture of a boy who sucked his thumb when he was a baby. 

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:08.460
Notice how the upper teeth protrude and the chin recedes.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.960
And see how his appearance has been improved by orthodontic treatment.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:23.160
This is a plaster of Paris model of a boy's
teeth before and after correction.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.140
[Tommy rests his chin on his hand.]

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:30.480
[Dr. Martin:] Now Tommy, you know that sleeping or resting the face on the hand 

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.960
may cause irregular jaws and teeth also.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:38.940
[ Music ]

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:42.420
[Narrator:] Now that Miss Young is back, the dentist invites his guests

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.580
to the lunch that has been set out in the back yard.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.400
[ Music ]

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:59.000
[A housekeeper is laying the table for lunch. There are a table, several chairs, and an umbrella shading the table. All sit down.]

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:05.200
[Narrator:] This properly balanced meal consists of celery, which exercises the jaws and teeth. 

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:12.340
A lettuce and tomato salad and milk, the most important of all foods. 

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:22.860
Deviled eggs. Whole grain bread and butter. And fruits complete the lunch.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:28.040
Since it is good practice to clean the teeth
following each meal, 

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:34.800
Miss Young offers to demonstrate an accepted method of tooth brushing.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.900
Let's hear what she says.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.540
[Miss Young:] Follow a regular toothbrushing method. 

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.960
And always begin at a definite place.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.700
[Miss Young holds an oversize model of the lower teeth and demonstrates proper brushing.]

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:53.280
[Miss Young:] Put the  brush high up on the gums, with the bristles pointing at the roots of the teeth.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:57.120
Use considerable pressure, brushing toward the chewing surfaces. 

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:02.100
This enables the bristles to penetrate and clean between the teeth.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.040
Continue around the mouth and repeat on the inside. 

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:10.740
Make eight to ten sweeps in the same location, and again on the lowers. 

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:15.060
Brush toward the chewing surfaces inside and outside. 

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:19.980
Use a back-and-forth [motion] -- and be sure to scrub them well.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.860
[ Music ]

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:29.280
[Tommy attempts to use the oversized toothbrush to brush the pony's teeth. Miss Young intervenes.]

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:36.400
[ Music ]

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:40.860
[Narrator:] With all that they have learned,
it is now easy as well as entertaining

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:44.340
for Mary Jane and Tommy to make their school project.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:55.120
[Mary Jane and Tommy work assiduously with paper and craft materials to complete their project.]

00:07:55.120 --> 00:08:01.680
[Narrator:] Even a neighbor's twins are inspected. What? No teeth?

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:08.640
[Mary Jane works on the scrapbook, lying on her bed.]

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.540
[ Music ]

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:19.540
[Tommy completes the final assembly and Mary Jane sits decisively on the scrapbook to set the glue.]

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:24.740
[Narrator:] With their scrapbook finished, they proudly
take it to school to present it to Miss Allen.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:29.960
[Children scramble up the schoolhouse steps to their classrooms.]

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.400
[Mary Jane and Tommy present the scrapbook to their teacher.] 

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:38.020
[The scrapbook is titled The Value of a Smile.]

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.020
[One of the first pages is a hand-drawn picture of the dentist with the words, "Our friend The Dentist (see him often)."]

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.720
[Next page is a hand-drawn picture of various fruits, vegetables, eggs, and a milk bottle.]

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.380
[Narrator:] The title of the book was "The Value of a Smile." We know how much a dollar is and how

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.540
[Next page is a hand-drawn picture of a tube of toothpaste, a toothbrush, and a tooth.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:47.600
[The final page in handwritten letters, "The
End."]

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:49.080
[Film ends abruptly.]

